From c0153f70b6f41482c2abec582c29463b75ee076d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:40:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-72: a new event is wired page -> server -> C++ by
 itself (htd.event) (0.72.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20260930: "如果我有需要新增事件 其他連結 理應外掛程式自動幫我新增" (and before:
"你用json中間連線的 是你這邊要幫我處理 我只需要處理C++的部分").
A double-click on an empty event (or a typed name) adds the C++ handler as
before AND, in the same edit, nothing saved:
- the page: one line in its <script id="htdEvents"> block --
  htdCpp('spbSave', 'dblclick', 'TfHotPlate', 'spbSaveDblClick', 'OnDblClick');
  -- and, once, the htdCpp helper: sends WS htd.event through the page's
  client (the loaded object with rawCmd; token first, like the page's own
  senders; a failure said on the page). The client script is added when the
  page does not load it.
- HtdEvents/HtdEvents.gen.cpp (new lib/cppbridge.js; an untitled document at
  that path, nothing on disk until saved): one row per designer event, calling
  the form's global object (fHotPlate->spbSaveDblClick(sender)); mouse button /
  position / Shift-Ctrl-Alt / key code from the page, by the declared
  parameters. Same rules as form.event, taken from its implementation: not
  while SystemStart / SoftStart, under ht9045::formjson::FormLock, cJSON.
- tools/wb_serve.cpp: the htd.event branch made from form.event's own (its
  checks, W906_HtdEvent, CompleteCommand), in front of it ON THE SAME LINE --
  no line moves; once.
- CMakeLists.txt: the generated file in wb_serve's add_executable, in front of
  its ")" (same line); once.
Not wired (said why, the handler still added): no global object, a parameter
the page cannot give, a non-public declaration, no form.event to copy.
A renamed handler's page line and generated row follow. The 事件表 row of a
designer event is ITS handler (not htd.event's entry point), read from the
open documents before they are saved. A form.event table row's function is
the one the server runs (&B_cbSelectHPFromDBChange's definition).

Checked by compiling (syntax only, in scratch; no build dir touched): the
generated file (WinLibs 16.2 C++14 and MinGW.org 6.3) and wb_serve.cpp with
the branch (a deliberately broken copy fails, so the branch is compiled).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 158, smoke 159, panels, real VS Code 147):
real VS Code (OnDblClick -> the page line, the redrawn page binds dblclick,
wb_serve.cpp / CMakeLists.txt dirty with the hooks, the generated file
untitled and not on disk; the row = spbSaveDblClick; all reverted; MD5 of
wb_serve.cpp / CMakeLists.txt / fHotPlate.h / .cpp unchanged), smoke (the
same in memory + rename follows), lib (server hook on the real wb_serve.cpp
keeps the line count, CMake hook, calls, generated file, page lines).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
